From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Bryan Hoban <bryan.hoban@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 14:14:40 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] Dolby Vision: carry stream and picture metadata through
 VideoPlayer

The plumbing the rest of the Dolby Vision series builds on:

- CDemuxStream and CDVDStreamInfo carry the enhancement layer's HEVC
  configuration record (doviELConfig, from the stream's
  AV_PKT_DATA_HEVC_CONF side data), compared and copied with the other
  extradata. The DOVI configuration record is only taken when it is
  whole.
- VideoPicture carries the picture's Dolby Vision RPU metadata
  (CDVMetadataBuffer: bounded, reference counted, sharing the frame's
  side-data buffer instead of copying it, as FFmpeg does not write it
  once attached), its source timestamp, its decoded enhancement-layer
  frame and whether a Profile 7 MEL's enhancement layer was skipped.

Everything but the metadata buffer and the timestamp is under
HAVE_DVBRIDGE, which kodi-9957 defines (ENABLE_DVBRIDGE). The decoder
(kodi-9952) fills these fields; the renderer (kodi-9956, kodi-9957)
reads them.

Formerly part of kodi-9990-native-dv, with yblod-24 (the MEL skip flag)
and yblod-58 (sharing the side-data buffer).
